---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { siteConfig } from "../config";
const BlueTuna_data = siteConfig.BlueTuna;

import MaxF1_bxplt from "../../public/MaxF1s_bxplt.png";
import PreProc_img from "../../public/preproc_image.png";
---

<!--title section-->
<section id="bluetuna" class="p-8 sm:p-12 md:p-16 lg:p-24">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:gap-16 items-start">
        <div class="lg:col-span-4">
            <h2
                class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl xl:text-7xl font-bold text-gray-900"
            >
                {BlueTuna_data.name}
            </h2>
            <div
                class="w-[300px] h-[10px] mt-2 rounded-full"
                style={`background-color: ${BlueTuna_data.color}`}
            >
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!--description and skills-->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start mt-6">
        <div>
            <p
                class={`text-lg font-mono sm:text-xl md:text-2xl leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mt-3 ${BlueTuna_data.repoLink ? "pr-12 sm:pr-14 md:pr-16" : ""}`}
            >
                {BlueTuna_data.description}
            </p>
            <p
                class={`text-lg font-mono sm:text-xl md:text-2xl leading-relaxed text-black mt-3 ${BlueTuna_data.repoLink ? "pr-12 sm:pr-14 md:pr-16" : ""}`}
            >
                Where traditional tuning libraries treat the search space as
                something to be continuously exploited, BlueTuna treats it as
                something to be understood beforehand. BlueTuna creatively
                addresses the task of hyperparameter optimization by breaking it
                down into 3 stages, each informing the next:
            </p>

            <ul
                class={`text-lg font-mono sm:text-xl md:text-2xl leading-relaxed text-gray mt-3 ${BlueTuna_data.repoLink ? "pr-12 sm:pr-14 md:pr-16" : ""}`}
            >
                <li>
                    [1] Parameter search space filtering via gradient-based
                    region scoring, isolates regions most likely to contain
                    performance optima
                </li>
                <li>
                    [2] Custom perceptron training on Latin Hypercube-sampled
                    data from filtered search space to better "see" the
                    hyperparameter landscape
                </li>
                <li>
                    [3] Fixed-weight gradient descent on hyperparameter values,
                    guiding model performance towards optima
                </li>
            </ul>

            <!--coloured divider-->
            <div
                class="w-[500px] h-[3px] mt-2 rounded-full"
                style={`background-color: ${BlueTuna_data.color}`}
            >
            </div>

            <p
                class={`text-lg font-mono sm:text-xl md:text-2xl leading-relaxed text-black mt-3 ${BlueTuna_data.repoLink ? "pr-12 sm:pr-14 md:pr-16" : ""}`}
            >
                BlueTuna was able to achieve a competitive performance ceiling
                against Optuna (top-performing optimizer), beating it on 5/20
                trials and competitive on 40%. Notably, its median performance
                slightly exceeded Optuna's, demonstrating its limitation to be
                consistency rather than performance ceiling.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 sm:gap-2 pt-2">
            <Image
                src={PreProc_img}
                alt="Stage 1 Conceptual Visualization"
                width="650"
            />
            <p>
                Gradient-based preprocessing concept visualization. The
                search space has been "split" by the fine dotted lines and
                gradients (dash lines) act as performance projections for each value region.
            </p>

            <!--coloured divider-->
            <div
                class="w-[650px] h-[3px] mt-2 rounded-full"
                style={`background-color: ${BlueTuna_data.color}`}
            >
            </div>

            <Image
                src={MaxF1_bxplt}
                alt="Max F1 benchmark boxplot"
                width="650"
            />
            {
                BlueTuna_data.skills.map((skill) => (
                    <span
                        class={`px-2.5 sm:px-3 py-1 sm:py-1.5 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-md sm:rounded-lg text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium transition-all duration-300 ${
                            BlueTuna_data.repoLink
                                ? "group-hover:bg-gray-800"
                                : ""
                        }`}
                    >
                        {skill}
                    </span>
                ))
            }
        </div>
    </div>

    <!--RepoLink box-->
    <div class="lg:col-span-8">
        <div class="space-y-8">
            <div class="group relative">
                <!--RepoBox-->
                <a
                    href={BlueTuna_data.repoLink}
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="group relative p-16 max-w-2x1 w-full"
                >
                    <div
                        class="relative p-8 md:p-16 bg-white rounded-3xl border-2 border-gray-200 shadow-lg transition-all duration-500 hover:shadow-2xl hover:-translate-y-2 hover:border-gray-300 mt-4"
                    >
                        <!-- Arrow icon in top-right -->
                        <div
                            class="absolute top-6 right-6 w-11 h-11 flex items-center justify-center bg-gray-900 rounded-full text-white transition-all duration-300 group-hover:bg-gray-700"
                            style={`background-color: ${BlueTuna_data.color}`}
                        >
                            <svg
                                class="w-5 h-5 transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-0.5 group-hover:-translate-y-0.5"
                                fill="none"
                                stroke="currentColor"
                                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                            >
                                <path
                                    stroke-linecap="round"
                                    stroke-linejoin="round"
                                    stroke-width="2"
                                    d="M7 17L17 7M17 7H7M17 7V17"></path>
                            </svg>
                        </div>

                        <div class="pr-24">
                            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
                                {BlueTuna_data.repoTitle}
                            </h3>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
